# Build context exclusions.
#
# Marzano does not ship a Docker image today, but a Dockerfile is a likely
# addition, and this file is the safety net that stops a build from baking
# credentials or runtime state into an image layer. Layer contents are visible
# to anyone who can pull the image, so this is a security boundary, not tidiness.

# Secrets - never in an image, under any circumstances
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
deploy_key
known_hosts.bak

# Runtime state
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
health.json*

# Build output and dependencies (rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests and tooling
tests/
scripts/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
coverage/
*.log
logs/

# Documentation is not needed at runtime
docs/
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md

# VCS and local noise
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.DS_Store
